From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] wsi/win32: Venus presents through a Direct3D 11 swap chain, on the GPU

Venus has no Direct3D 12 queue for DXGI, so its presents took the CPU path: each frame read back into memory and
drawn with GDI's StretchDIBits, ~1 ms at 1080p and 1.6 ms at 1440p. With Venus (and the GPU driver's Direct3D 11
driver) each swapchain image now has a shared Direct3D 11 RGBA8 texture whose host storage is Vulkan memory (mesa
patch 0035, virglrenderer 0012/0017); Venus imports it by its host resource id (the kernel driver's VIOGPU_RES_INFO
escape, VkImportMemoryResourceInfoMESA). A present blits the app's image into it on the app's queue (vkCmdBlitImage:
BGRA to RGBA), and the present thread copies it into a flip-model DXGI swap chain's buffer and presents: 0.41 ms at
1080p, 0.44 ms at 1440p. FIFO presents with sync interval 1, IMMEDIATE tears where DXGI allows it.

Anything missing (no Direct3D 11 device, the host without VK_SHARED, the import failing) falls back to the CPU path
per surface; WINBOAT_VK_PRESENT=copy forces it.
---
diff --git a/src/vulkan/wsi/meson.build b/src/vulkan/wsi/meson.build
index 80925d1..51c9abe 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/meson.build
+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/meson.build
@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@ if with_platform_wayland
 endif
 
